{"name":"Butterfly Bush","hex":"#68578c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"butterfly bush","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several plants that conspicuously attract butterflies.\n Any buddleia, of genus Buddleja.\nEspecially, one of the species Buddleja davidii or Buddleja globosa.\n Blue butterfly bush (Rotheca myricoides, syn. Clerodendrum ugandense).\n The butterfly weed (Asclepias tuberosa).","Any buddleia, of genus Buddleja.\nEspecially, one of the species Buddleja davidii or Buddleja globosa."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/butterfly_bush"}],"entries":[{"title":"Butterfly bush","blocks":[{"text":"Butterfly bush may refer to a number of different plants including:"},{"items":["Buddleja\nBuddleja davidii\nBuddleja globosa","Buddleja davidii","Buddleja globosa","Rotheca myricoides, native to Africa"]},{"items":["Buddleja davidii","Buddleja globosa"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butterfly_bush","wikidata":"Q5002966"},{"title":"Butterfly","blocks":[{"text":"Butterflies are winged insects from the lepidopteran superfamily Papilionoidea, characterised by large, often brightly coloured wings that often fold together when at rest, and a conspicuous, fluttering flight. The oldest butterfly fossils have been dated to the Paleocene, about 56 million years ago, though molecular evidence suggests that they likely originated in the Cretaceous."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Fesoj_-_Papilio_machaon_%28by%29.jpg/330px-Fesoj_-_Papilio_machaon_%28by%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butterfly","wikidata":"Q11946202"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Common_brimstone_butterfly_%28Gonepteryx_rhamni%29_male_in_flight.jpg/500px-Common_brimstone_butterfly_%28Gonepteryx_rhamni%29_male_in_flight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_con